title: OPNsense: DHCP Pool Usage
agents: opnsense
catalog: os/networking
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk

description:
 This check monitors the usage of a DHCPv4 address pool of Kea DHCP or
 Dnsmasq on an OPNsense firewall. The data is collected via the special agent
 {agent_opnsense} from the {kea/dhcpv4/search_subnet}, {kea/leases4/search},
 {dnsmasq/settings/search_range} and {dnsmasq/leases/search} endpoints.
 The API user needs "Services: DHCP: Kea(v4)" and/or "Services: Dnsmasq
 DNS/DHCP: Settings" - both also allow configuration changes and service
 restarts of the respective DHCP server.

 Used addresses are the active leases inside the pool range; static
 reservations outside the range are not counted. Default levels are
 80 / 90 percent and can be set through the rule "OPNsense DHCP pool usage".
 The legacy ISC DHCP server is not supported.

item:
 The backend and subnet or range, for example {Kea 192.168.1.0/24}.

discovery:
 One service {OPNsense DHCP Pool ITEM} is created for each configured pool.
